    <!-- Test-app mark, light mode. Compiled ONLY under -PtestApp (see the conditional res
         srcDir in app/build.gradle.kts); production never reads this directory.

         ⚠️ This replaces an override of the BACKGROUND, which used to be a loud amber tile.
         Two things killed that. Brandon objected to the colour on sight ("shouldnt be
         orange"), and once the real icon gained a light/dark pair the background was no
         longer free to borrow: a test build overriding only drawable/ would have been marked
         in light mode and silently unmarked in dark.

         So the marker moved to the mark itself and went greyscale. It reads instantly as
         "not the real one", it spends no colour at all (which matters now that the tile IS
         the brand), and greyscale works against both tiles, so the test build stays marked
         in both themes. Greys are luminance matches for the colours they stand in for, and
         the light/dark inversion of the lit pair is preserved: see
         drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml in main for the rule. -->

